# Build output and local scratch.
.tmp/
node_modules/
*.log

# The edge Worker is deliberately NOT tracked.
#
# `wrangler.toml` names `worker.js` as the module entrypoint, but the file
# itself stays out of git on purpose: it pins the commit whose assets the
# Worker serves, and that pin is bumped by hand for every deploy. Tracking it
# would put the Worker and the assets it serves in the same commit, and the
# Worker would then serve the commit that contains it. That coupling broke on
# 2026-10-08.
#
# The deployed source is maintained in the workspace working copy
# (projects/loopwise-health/worker.js) and uploaded with a multipart modules
# PUT. See the site README's Deploy section.
worker.js
